  "id": "COMPOUND:15910 - PROTEIN:6138",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 9-Angeloylretronecine and the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, mediated through multiple targets. The drug 9-Angeloylretronecine is identified as a target of several entities, including Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like and (1R,3R,4S,7S,9S,11S,13R,14R,15R)-4,11,13,14-tetrahydroxy-7-[(2Z,4R)-4-(hydroxymethyl)hex-2-en-2-yl]-3,9,15-trimethoxy-12,12-dimethyl-6,17-dioxabicyclo[11.3.1]heptadecan-5-one. These targets are all known to interact with the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, indicating a possible pathway where 9-Angeloylretronecine influences the proteasome’s function. The evidence is consistent across different targets, suggesting that the drug may modulate the proteasome’s activity through these intermediaries. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for 9-Angeloylretronecine in regulating proteasome function, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
